---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';

const lastUpdated = 'September 2026';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy · Luma Pediatrics"
  path="/privacy"
  description="Privacy policy for Luma Pediatrics in McKinney, TX. How we collect, use, and protect information submitted through our website."
>
  <section class="page-hero py-14 md:py-20 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center fade-up">
      <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
      <h1 class="mt-5 text-4xl md:text-5xl tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted-foreground)]">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pb-20 md:pb-28 reveal">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 prose-luma">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how Luma Pediatrics ("we," "us," "our") handles
        information submitted through our website at {SITE.domain}. When clinical services begin,
        protected health information ("PHI") will be handled separately under our Notice of Privacy
        Practices (HIPAA).
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
      <p>
        We collect the email address, optional name, consent selection, source page, and submission
        time that you voluntarily provide through the practice-updates form. This signup is not
        patient registration and does not establish a physician-patient relationship.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you contact us by phone, text, or email, we may collect your contact information, the
        content of the communication, and related customer care records. Please do not include
        medical information in these communications.
      </p>
      <p>
        We also collect technical and usage information automatically, such as IP address, browser
        and device type, referring URL, pages visited, and approximate location.
      </p>

      <h2>2. How we use information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To respond to general customer care questions.</li>
        <li>To send occasional updates about the planned opening and general services.</li>
        <li>To manage consent and honor HELP, STOP, unsubscribe, correction, and deletion requests.</li>
        <li>To operate, secure, analyze, and improve the website.</li>
        <li>To comply with applicable law.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. How we share information</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell personal information. We may share information with service providers that
        support website hosting, analytics, communications, and data storage, but only as needed to
        provide those services. We may also disclose information when required by law, to protect
        rights or safety, or in connection with a business reorganization.
      </p>

      <h2>4. SMS Communications</h2>
      <p>
        Luma Pediatrics uses SMS to provide customer care communications to individuals who choose
        to communicate with us by text. Message frequency varies. Message and data rates may apply.
        You may reply HELP for assistance or STOP to opt out.
      </p>
      <p>
        Mobile information will not be shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or
        promotional purposes. Text messaging originator opt-in data and consent will not be shared
        with third parties.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not share or transfer consumer SMS data or registration information to any external
        organizations, except where disclosure is legally required.
      </p>
      <p>
        Consumer consent does not permit or override any prohibited sharing or transfer of consumer
        SMS data or registration information.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Safeguards We Use</strong></p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Access controls that limit consumer SMS data and registration information to authorized
          personnel only.
        </li>
        <li>Internal privacy procedures designed to prevent unauthorized use or disclosure.</li>
        <li>
          Security measures maintained to protect consumer SMS data and registration information
          from unauthorized disclosure.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If you have questions regarding our SMS communications or privacy practices, please contact
        Luma Pediatrics through the contact information provided on our website.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Cookies & analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Our website uses Google Analytics to understand site traffic and performance. Analytics may
        collect information such as device type, approximate location, referring page, and pages
        visited. Google may process this information under its own privacy terms. You can limit
        cookies through your browser settings or use available browser privacy controls.
      </p>

      <h2>6. HIPAA and medical information</h2>
      <p>
        Luma Pediatrics is not currently open or providing clinical services. This website, the
        practice-updates form, email, and SMS are not intended for medical advice, patient
        registration, or the collection of protected health information. Please do not send
        symptoms, diagnoses, medications, insurance member IDs, medical records, or other clinical
        information through these channels.
      </p>
      <p>
        When clinical services begin, protected health information handled in connection with care
        will be governed by applicable law, including HIPAA, and our
        {' '}<a href="/notice-of-privacy-practices/">Notice of Privacy Practices</a>. Information that
        is not protected health information remains subject to this Privacy Policy. For current care,
        contact your existing healthcare provider. For a medical emergency, call 911.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain information only as reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this policy,
        including maintaining consent and opt-out records, responding to requests, operating the
        website, and meeting legal obligations. Retention periods may vary by record type.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our website is directed to parents and guardians, not children. We do not knowingly collect
        personal information directly from children under 13 through this website. If you believe a
        child has submitted personal information, contact us so we can review the request.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational safeguards appropriate to
        the information we maintain. No method of internet transmission or storage is completely
        secure, so we cannot guarantee absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You may unsubscribe from updates at any time or request access to, correction of, or deletion
        of information submitted through the website by emailing
        {' '}<a href={SITE.contact.emailHref}>{SITE.contact.email}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        For SMS customer care communications, reply HELP for assistance or STOP to opt out. We may
        retain an opt-out record to honor your request.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Third-party links and services</h2>
      <p>
        The website may link to third-party websites or services. Their privacy practices are
        governed by their own policies, and Luma Pediatrics is not responsible for their content or
        privacy practices.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date above will reflect changes.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy? Email <a href={SITE.contact.emailHref}>{SITE.contact.email}</a>
        or write to {SITE.name}, {SITE.address.street}, {SITE.address.city}, {SITE.address.region} {SITE.address.postalCode}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose-luma h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-foreground);
  }
  .prose-luma p,
  .prose-luma li {
    color: rgba(11, 29, 58, 0.85);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }
  .prose-luma ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }
  .prose-luma a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
